Export:
To export configuration data, you need two main things:

    1)Schema XML containing which tables/columns you want.
    2)An output location where PAC should create the exported ZIP.

The schema XML is the part you create first, usually with the Configuration Migration Tool.

How to create the schema
    Open Configuration Migration Tool.
    Choose Create schema.
    Sign in to your Dataverse environment.
    Select your solution, for example: Budget Approval
    Select the table you want, for example: Approval Configuration
    Select the required columns, for example:
        Name
        Approval Level
        Minimum Amount
        Maximum Amount
        Approver
    Add related tables/relationships if required.
    Validate the schema.
    Save the schema.
ex:
        pac data export --schemaFile "C:\Data\ApprovalSchema.xml" --dataFile "C:\Data\ApprovalData.zip"

Import:
ex:
        pac data import --data "C:\Data\ApprovalData.zip"
During import we just need to connect to that environment and need to run the command Schema will be taken care this time.
